ous form of "the base is shared" -- the d^2 term appears ONCE for a list of ANY length. Scope as THEOREMS: lowRankUpdate_gauge (for any invertible r x r change of basis S the pair (A*S, S-inv*B) is the SAME update, so the proof binds the d x d DELTA and the factorization is gauge -- nothing may read A as "the adapter") and lowRank_blind_to_the_projection (whether A,B is the correct low-rank projection of the true gradient is a SEPARATE obligation). F5 teeth at a 4x4 layer with a rank-2 update: the SHARP one is lowRank_refuses_another_low_rank_update -- a genuinely different rank-2 delta is REFUSED, so what is certified is THIS delta and not "the delta is low rank"; plus a tampered base refused, the TRANSPOSED update refused (an index-order bug survives every symmetric test), the inference identity computed with the adapter shown to actually move the output, and the two-step chain computed. gauge_changes_the_factor + gauge_leaves_the_update_fixed exhibit a NONIDENTITY S the check cannot see, so the gauge scope item bounds a real freedom. Counting teeth at 2x2 with a rank-1 update cover the whole 25-point challenge space: 9 of 25 false accepts against the theorem's 10/25 (nearly ATTAINED, not slack), 16 refusals, and a tampered base accepted at 0 of 25
